     "interaction": "other",
     "effect": "inhibits",
     "mechanism": "Metformin lowers mTORC1 activity indirectly and does not bind mTOR. One route is AMPK-dependent, through phosphorylation of Raptor at Ser792 and enhancement of TSC2 GAP activity; a second is AMPK-independent, requires the Rag GTPases and was demonstrated in cells lacking AMPK or TSC2. Because of the second route, suppression of mTORC1 cannot be inferred from AMPK activation alone.",
