     "interaction": "drug_inhibition",
     "effect": "inhibits",
     "mechanism": "Because the ATP site is shared by both complexes and is not occluded by Rictor or mSin1, vistusertib inhibits mTORC2 as completely as mTORC1, abolishing AKT Ser473 phosphorylation; this is the source of the added metabolic toxicity of the ATP-competitive class.",
