     "target": "FRB_DOMAIN",
     "interaction": "binding",
     "effect": "inhibits",
     "mechanism": "The composite FKBP12-rapamycin surface wedges into the FRB domain adjacent to the catalytic cleft, narrowing substrate access; this gain-of-function mechanism explains why rapamycin is an allosteric, substrate-selective inhibitor rather than an ATP-competitive one.",
     "evidence": "established",
     "sites": [],
     "refs": [
