     "target": "PHENO_OLIGODENDROCYTE_DIFFERENTIATION",
     "interaction": "physiological_output",
     "effect": "required_for",
     "mechanism": "mTOR signalling is required for oligodendrocyte differentiation and myelination. Loss of Raptor delays the onset of myelination, reduces sheath thickness and impairs differentiation in a region-dependent manner, most severely in spinal cord, whereas loss of Rictor has modest effects and combined loss is most severe, so mTORC1 is dominant and mTORC2 contributory.",
     "evidence": "established",
