     "interaction": "physiological_output",
     "effect": "required_for",
     "mechanism": "Proliferating haematopoietic progenitors require mTORC1, which accounts for the cytopenias seen during rapalog therapy. Restraint of mTORC1 by the TSC complex is conversely required to keep haematopoietic stem cells quiescent: Tsc1 deletion drives stem cells out of quiescence, increases mitochondrial biogenesis and reactive oxygen species, and impairs self-renewal, so the compartment requires calibrated rather than maximal activity.",
