     "mechanism": "Conditional Rictor deletion in the postnatal murine forebrain selectively impairs long-term memory while sparing short-term memory; conversely, a compound that raises mTORC2 activity converts early-phase into late-phase potentiation, enhances long-term memory in wild-type animals and reverses age-associated memory impairment in mice and flies.",
