     "source": "MTORC2",
     "target": "TISSUE_CNS_NEURON",
     "interaction": "physiological_output",
     "effect": "required_for",
     "mechanism": "Conditional deletion of Rictor in the postnatal murine forebrain reduces mTORC2 activity and selectively impairs late-phase long-term potentiation and long-term memory while sparing early-phase potentiation and short-term memory; the mechanism is Tiam1–Rac1-dependent actin polymerisation with reduced dendritic spine density, and raising mTORC2 activity pharmacologically enhances long-term memory and reverses its age-associated decline.",
