     "mechanism": "S6K1 activity is required for mTOR-dependent phosphorylation of the UBF carboxy-terminal activation domain, which enhances UBF binding to SL1 and Pol I transcription of rDNA. Rapamycin causes rapid dephosphorylation of this domain, and a constitutively active, rapamycin-resistant S6K1 reverses it. Direct phosphorylation of UBF by S6K1 has not been shown, so the relationship is S6K1-dependent rather than a proven kinase-substrate interaction.",
